# suite=run; columns: <FAULT_ID> <must-fail> <allowed-prefixes> <must-pass>
# Run named faults (plan 04-06, D-08). Each id has one IVS_FAULT_<ID> site in
# core/src/machine/machine_inspect.c (observation must not disturb what it observes).
# PEEK_ADVANCES_TIME: every accepted peek adds one master tick to machine time; both side-effect
# cases see the storage, the INSTANCE and composite digests and machine time change.
PEEK_ADVANCES_TIME run.observe.no-side-effect-powered run.observe.|run.peek.|run.refuse.peek. run.cpu-state.off
# PEEK_GATE_IGNORED: peek reads the backing word as if every gate were open; only the closed-gate
# case sees GROM and GRAM data behind gate gmem.
PEEK_GATE_IGNORED run.peek.gated run.peek.gated run.peek.loaded-words
# Run-bound faults (plan 04-07, D-07), one site each in core/src/machine/machine_bound.c (the run
# loop must neither run past its target range, stop short of the target nor step a faulted CPU).
# RUN_TARGET_UNCHECKED: the OUT_OF_RANGE stage is skipped; the refusal case tries the targets on a
# FAULTED CPU first, so the run ends at once with IVS_OK (never a run toward 2^64).
RUN_TARGET_UNCHECKED run.refuse.target-above-2-63 run.refuse.target-above-2-63 run.stop-name.known
# RUN_STOP_BEFORE_OVERSHOOT: a unit that would end past the target is taken back (CPU and time),
# so the run stops at the last boundary below the target. Collateral by the same rule: every case
# whose target lies inside a unit (overshoot window, run(now + 1), the idle target h + 41, and the
# positive controls of report-inside-instance and tail-nonzero that expect now >= 1000).
RUN_STOP_BEFORE_OVERSHOOT run.target.ends-at-first-boundary-ge-target run.target.|run.overshoot.|run.single-step.|run.stop.halt-no-flag|run.refuse.report-inside-instance|run.refuse.tail-nonzero run.stop-name.known
# RUN_FAULT_STEPS: a FAULTED CPU is stepped (a zero-progress unit, counted) and the stop order
# tests the target before the fault, so a fault on the target boundary reports TARGET and later
# calls execute a unit. Collateral: every guest-fault stop case and the 2^63 boundary on a
# faulted CPU (an extra unit).
RUN_FAULT_STEPS run.stop.fault-sticky run.stop.|run.target.max-accepted run.cpu-state.off
